From 38090c65745836e844e7c1c37a96bc56e11175af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Cheng <chengyuejia@foxmail.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 22:37:03 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(knorm): converge activation to single should_activate()
 source of truth
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Address reviewer feedback on PR #209: the runner-side _knorm_active
condition was incomplete (missing compression_ratio < 1.0 check from
KnormConfig.is_active), risking another half-enabled state when
compression_ratio=1.0.

Changes:
- Add should_activate(enable_prefix_caching) to vllm/knorm/config.py as
  the single source of truth, checking VLLM_KNORM_ENABLED AND
  compression_ratio < 1.0 AND not enable_prefix_caching
- register_all_kvcache_specs now calls should_activate() instead of
  inline envs checks
- gpu_model_runner._knorm_active now calls should_activate() instead of
  inline envs checks
- Add test_knorm_coverage_matrix: 8 combinations of Knorm on/off ×
  prefix caching on/off × compression_ratio 0.5/1.0, verifying both
  should_activate() and register_all_kvcache_specs agree on manager type
- Add test_knorm_is_not_registered_when_compression_ratio_is_one
- Update test_knorm_runner_static.py to verify should_activate() is used

Refs #163
